  "derivation": "Foundation 35 GameComponentCollection. The contract row is read from the pinned XNA 4.0 Windows metadata. The ordering rows are read from the pinned Microsoft.Xna.Framework.Game.dll IL: InsertItem checks IndexOf != -1 and throws before base.InsertItem, then raises ComponentAdded only when the item is non-null; RemoveItem reads base[index] before base.RemoveItem and raises ComponentRemoved after it, again only when non-null; SetItem is newobj NotSupportedException + throw with no branch at all; ClearItems raises ComponentRemoved for every element -- with no null check -- re-reading base.Count on each iteration, and calls base.ClearItems only afterwards. The base-class conditions are read from the admitted Microsoft mscorlib Collection`1. The RUBY_MAPPING_QUALIFICATION rows record the projection decisions -- the CLR base really being a Ruby superclass, the declared generic element type, and the established event primitive -- and are not snapshotted from the cna-ruby implementation.",
